.\" Generated from wwal.1.scd
.TH "WWAL" "1" "2026-10-30" "wwal 1.2.0" "WayWal Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
wwal - zero-copy Wayland wallpaper, VA-API video, Shadertoy, and Material You client
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBwwal\fR [GLOBAL OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [ARGUMENTS...]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBwwal\fR is the command-line controller for \fBwwald\fR(1), a C23 Wayland wallpaper engine that unifies static DMA-BUF wallpapers, 18 GLES 3.1 compute shader transitions, zero-FFmpeg VA-API hardware video playback, live Shadertoy fragment/compute shaders with PipeWire 64-bin Bark FFT audio reactivity, Steam Wallpaper Engine (\fB431960\fR) Workshop scenes, and sub-millisecond dual-mode OKLab/CAM16/HCT Material Design 3 color extraction and template rendering.
.PP
When invoked via a symlink named \fBswww\fR, \fBawww\fR, \fBswww-daemon\fR, or \fBawww-daemon\fR, \fBwwal\fR automatically enables full command-line, environment variable, and cache-file compatibility with \fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR v0.12.1 scripts, GUI pickers, and launchers.
.PP
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-j, --json\fR
.RS 4
Format \fBquery\fR, \fBstatus\fR, and \fBstats\fR output as structured JSON.
.RE
.PP
\fB-n, --namespace\fR <NAME>
.RS 4
Connect to the daemon socket namespace \fINAME\fR (default: \fBdefault\fR). Also sets the Wayland layer-shell namespace unless overridden.
.RE
.PP
\fB-a, --all\fR
.RS 4
Broadcast the command to all active \fBwwald\fR daemon namespaces discovered in \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR (optionally filtered by \fBWWAL_NAMESPACE_PREFIX\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB-q, --quiet\fR
.RS 4
Suppress non-error informational output.
.RE
.PP
\fB-d, --daemon\fR
.RS 4
Fork \fBwwald\fR into the background when invoked with \fBinit\fR, \fBdaemon\fR, \fBswww-daemon\fR, or \fBawww-daemon\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fB--no-daemon\fR
.RS 4
Keep \fBwwald\fR in the foreground (\fBswww-daemon\fR / \fBawww-daemon\fR compatibility).
.RE
.PP
\fB-f, --format\fR <xrgb|xbgr|rgb|bgr>
.RS 4
Pixel channel order hint when launching \fBwwald\fR (\fBswww-daemon\fR / \fBawww-daemon\fR compatibility).
.RE
.PP
\fB-v, --verbose\fR
.RS 4
Enable verbose diagnostic output.
.RE
.PP
\fB-V, --version\fR
.RS 4
Print version information and exit.
.RE
.PP
\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS 4
Display usage information and exit.
.RE
.PP
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
\fBimg\fR <PATH|-> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Universal wallpaper command. Automatically detects and dispatches static or animated images (PNG, JPEG, WebP, AVIF, HEIC/HEIF, JPEG-XL, SVG, BMP, GIF, APNG, QOI, PPM/PGM/PNM, TGA), hardware videos (MP4, WebM, MKV, MOV, AVI, M4V), live shaders (\fB.frag\fR, \fB.comp\fR, \fB.glsl\fR, \fB.shader\fR), Steam Workshop numeric IDs, Workshop folders, or synced preview symlinks, GNOME dynamic timed wallpaper XML schedules (\fB.xml\fR), slideshow directories, and solid hex colors. Pass \fB-\fR to read image bytes from standard input. File descriptors are passed to \fBwwald\fR(1) via \fBSCM_RIGHTS\fR for zero-copy decoding inside the sandbox.
.RE
.PP
\fBpick\fR [DIR] [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Launch a unified icon-grid wallpaper picker across static images, videos, shaders, and Steam Workshop scenes. Automatically generates cached \fB128x128\fR / \fB160x90\fR thumbnails in \fB~/.cache/wwal/thumbs/\fR and pipes icon-annotated entries into \fBrofi\fR, \fBfuzzel\fR, \fBwalker\fR, or \fBdmenu\fR. Use \fB--menu <auto|rofi|fuzzel|walker|dmenu|stdout|json>\fR to select the output protocol and \fB--dir <DIR>\fR to add search directories.
.RE
.PP
\fBvideo\fR <PATH> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Play a hardware-accelerated video wallpaper (MP4, WebM, MKV, MOV, AVI, M4V, GIF) using the zero-FFmpeg MP4/WebM demuxer and VA-API hardware decode pipeline (H.264, HEVC, VP9, AV1).
.RE
.PP
\fBshader\fR <PATH|list|preset> [NAME] [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Run a live procedural GLSL compute shader (\fB.comp\fR), multi-pass Shadertoy fragment shader (\fB.frag\fR) with automatic \fBinotify\fR(7) hot-reloading, or one of 10 built-in procedural shader presets installed in \fBshaders/presets/*.frag\fR. Use \fBwwal shader list\fR (or \fB--list\fR) to list built-in presets (\fBaurora\fR, \fBcyber_grid\fR, \fBfluid_ink\fR, \fBsynthwave_sun\fR, \fBstarfield\fR, \fBrain_glass\fR, \fBaudio_bars\fR, \fBaudio_ring\fR, \fBcrt_retro\fR, \fBplasma_orb\fR, plus aliases \fBlava_lamp\fR, \fBnorthern_lights\fR, \fBoutrun\fR, \fBcrt\fR) and \fBwwal shader preset <NAME>\fR (or \fB--preset <NAME>\fR) to launch one directly.
.RE
.PP
\fBworkshop\fR <list|info|apply|sync-previews> [ID|PATH] [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Discover, inspect, render, or export preview symlinks for native Steam Workshop (\fB431960\fR Wallpaper Engine) scenes, videos, web wallpapers, `.pkg` archives, `.tex` textures, `.mdl` Puppet Warp skeletal meshes, AVX2 particle systems, `"sound"` ambient audio layers, `"text"` clock/label layers, and `SceneScript` logic. Use \fB--prop key=val\fR to override user properties, or \fBwwal workshop sync-previews [DIR]\fR to populate human-readable preview symlinks in \fB~/.cache/wwal/workshop-previews/\fR for external GUI pickers (\fBwaypaper\fR, \fBazote\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBslideshow\fR <DIR|FILE.xml|ACTION> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Start a zero-idle-CPU \fBtimerfd\fR mixed-media wallpaper slideshow from \fIDIR\fR or a GNOME timed dynamic wallpaper schedule (\fIFILE.xml\fR), or control an active slideshow using one of the actions: \fBstart\fR, \fBstop\fR, \fBpause\fR, \fBresume\fR, \fBtoggle\fR, \fBnext\fR, \fBprev\fR, \fBprevious\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBnext\fR [-o <OUTPUT>]
.RS 4
Advance the active slideshow on the target output(s) to the next wallpaper.
.RE
.PP
\fBprev\fR, \fBprevious\fR [-o <OUTPUT>]
.RS 4
Return the active slideshow on the target output(s) to the previous wallpaper.
.RE
.PP
\fBcolor\fR <HEX> [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Set the target output(s) to a solid RGB/RGBA hex color (for example, \fB#1e1e2e\fR or \fB1e1e2eff\fR) using \fBwp_single_pixel_buffer_v1\fR when supported by the compositor.
.RE
.PP
\fBclear\fR [HEX] [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Alias for \fBcolor\fR (defaults to \fB000000\fR if no color is given) for \fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility.
.RE
.PP
\fBtheme\fR [PATH] [-i|--img|--image <PATH>] [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Extract simultaneous dark and light OKLab/CAM16/HCT Material Design 3 palettes from \fIPATH\fR (or via \fB-i, --img, --image <PATH>\fR, or the currently active wallpaper if omitted) in under 0.5 ms, render all configured \fB[template."<name>"]\fR files (supporting Matugen, Wallust, and Pywal syntax and 7 pipe filters), and write \fB~/.local/state/caelestia/scheme.json\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors.{json,css,hyprland.conf}\fR, \fB~/.cache/wal/{colors.json,colors,colors.sh,colors.css,sequences}\fR, and terminal OSC 4/10/11 sequences.
.RE
.PP
\fBaudio\fR [OPTIONS]
.RS 4
Configure live wallpaper audio playback volume (\fB--volume 0.0..1.0\fR) and external application auto-ducking (\fB--mute-on-audio\fR / \fB--no-mute-on-audio\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBset-uniform\fR, \fBuniform\fR <NAME> <VALUES...>
.RS 4
Mutate a live shader uniform or Workshop user property (1 to 4 float values) without reloading the active scene.
.RE
.PP
\fBstatus\fR [--json]
.RS 4
Inspect connected outputs, active wallpaper/video/shader/Workshop paths, D-Bus MPRIS2 media metadata, and daemon telemetry.
.RE
.PP
\fBsubscribe\fR
.RS 4
Stream newline-delimited JSON events whenever wallpapers, themes, or media states change.
.RE
.PP
\fBpause\fR
.RS 4
Pause active video, animation, live shader, or Workshop scene playback.
.RE
.PP
\fBresume\fR, \fBunpause\fR
.RS 4
Resume paused video, animation, live shader, or Workshop scene playback.
.RE
.PP
\fBtoggle\fR
.RS 4
Toggle video, animation, live shader, or Workshop scene playback between paused and playing states.
.RE
.PP
\fBquery\fR [--json]
.RS 4
List all connected Wayland outputs, physical and logical dimensions, scale factors, refresh rates, and active wallpaper state.
.RE
.PP
\fBstats\fR [--json]
.RS 4
Query real-time daemon telemetry (opcode \fB0x000C\fR), including daemon RSS/PSS memory footprint, active VRAM surface pool count, negotiated DRM FourCC format and modifier (Linear, NVIDIA Block-Linear, ARM AFBC, AMD DCC, Intel CCS), VBlank PLL period/phase jitter estimates, and per-output Zero-Watt \fBpause_mask\fR reasons.
.RE
.PP
\fBrestore\fR
.RS 4
Restore the last persisted per-output wallpaper, video, shader, Workshop scene, or color state from \fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/wwal/state.bin\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBclear-cache\fR
.RS 4
Remove cached hardware-transcoded animations, thumbnails, and palette artifacts from \fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/wwal\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBinit\fR, \fBdaemon\fR
.RS 4
Launch or initialize the \fBwwald\fR(1) daemon (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility alias).
.RE
.PP
\fBping\fR
.RS 4
Check whether \fBwwald\fR(1) is running and responsive over the IPC socket.
.RE
.PP
\fBkill\fR
.RS 4
Gracefully terminate the running \fBwwald\fR(1) daemon.
.RE
.PP
\fBversion\fR
.RS 4
Print version information and exit.
.RE
.PP
\fBhelp\fR
.RS 4
Show command-line usage summary.
.RE
.PP
.SH IMAGE & TRANSITION OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-t, --transition-type\fR <TYPE>
.RS 4
Select transition effect (default: \fBfade\fR). Supported GPU GLES 3.1 compute shader and AVX-512/AVX2/NEON SIMD transition types:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnone\fR: Instant buffer swap with zero transition frames.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsimple\fR: Linear alpha cross-dissolve.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfade\fR: Cubic-bezier eased alpha crossfade.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwipe\fR: Directional linear edge wipe controlled by \fB--transition-angle\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgrow\fR: Expanding circular iris anchored at \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBouter\fR: Contracting circular iris toward \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBwave\fR: Sinusoidal wave front controlled by \fB--transition-wave\fR and \fB--transition-angle\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnoise\fR: Perlin/simplex procedural noise dissolve.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcrosszoom\fR: Radial motion-blur zoom crossfade.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBslide\fR: Directional viewport push transition.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBglitch\fR: RGB chromatic aberration and block-shift digital glitch.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBburn\fR: Procedural ember/fire edge burn.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBripple\fR: Concentric water ripple refraction anchored at \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpixelate\fR: Dynamic mosaic block quantization transition.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdoom\fR: Classic vertical column melt transition.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBswirl\fR: Spiral vortex distortion around \fB--transition-pos\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcube\fR: 3D perspective rotating cube face transition.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBluma\fR: Luminance threshold ramp transition.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlight_leak\fR: Warm filmic anamorphic flare transition.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpage_curl\fR: 3D cylindrical page curl with specular shading.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcustom\fR: User-supplied GLSL compute shader via \fB--transition-shader\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, \fBtop\fR, \fBbottom\fR: Directional slide transition aliases (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcenter\fR, \fBany\fR: Centered or arbitrary radial iris grow aliases (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrandom\fR: Randomly choose one of the 18 built-in shader transitions.
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-duration\fR <SECONDS>
.RS 4
Duration of the transition in seconds as a floating-point number such as \fB0.5\fR or \fB1.5\fR (default: \fB1.2\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-fps\fR <FPS>
.RS 4
Target transition frame rate (default: \fB60\fR; automatically locks to display VBlank via \fBwp_presentation\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-bezier\fR <X1,Y1,X2,Y2>
.RS 4
Cubic Bezier control points for transition progress easing (default: \fB0.25,0.1,0.25,1.0\fR; \fBswww\fR default: \fB0.54,0,0.34,0.99\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-angle\fR <DEGREES>
.RS 4
Direction angle in degrees for \fBwipe\fR, \fBwave\fR, and \fBslide\fR transitions (default: \fB0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-wave\fR <FREQ,AMP>
.RS 4
Frequency and amplitude for the \fBwave\fR transition (default: \fB20,0.05\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-pos\fR <POS>
.RS 4
Anchor position for \fBgrow\fR, \fBouter\fR, \fBripple\fR, and \fBswirl\fR transitions. Accepts normalized coordinates \fBX,Y\fR in \fB0.0..1.0\fR, percentage coordinates (\fB50%,50%\fR), pixel offsets, or semantic aliases: \fBcenter\fR, \fBtop\fR, \fBbottom\fR, \fBleft\fR, \fBright\fR, \fBtop-left\fR (\fBtl\fR, \fBtopleft\fR), \fBtop-right\fR (\fBtr\fR, \fBtopright\fR), \fBbottom-left\fR (\fBbl\fR, \fBbottomleft\fR), \fBbottom-right\fR (\fBbr\fR, \fBbottomright\fR), \fBcursor\fR, \fBmouse\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fB--invert-y\fR
.RS 4
Invert the Y coordinate of \fB--transition-pos\fR (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility).
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-step\fR <STEP>
.RS 4
Per-frame progress step (\fB1..255\fR) for \fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility.
.RE
.PP
\fB--transition-shader\fR <FILE>
.RS 4
Path to a custom GLSL ES 3.10 compute shader (\fB.comp\fR) when \fB--transition-type custom\fR is selected.
.RE
.PP
\fB-o, --output, --outputs\fR <NAMES>
.RS 4
Target specific Wayland output(s) by name (for example, \fBDP-1\fR or \fBDP-1,HDMI-A-1\fR). May be specified multiple times.
.RE
.PP
\fB--sync-mode\fR <simultaneous|staggered>
.RS 4
Synchronize transitions across multiple monitors simultaneously or with a cascading delay (default: \fBsimultaneous\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--stagger-delay\fR <MS>
.RS 4
Cascading delay in milliseconds between outputs when \fB--sync-mode staggered\fR is active (default: \fB150\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--scaling-mode, --mode, --resize\fR <MODE>
.RS 4
Aspect-ratio scaling mode:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfill\fR, \fBcrop\fR, \fBcover\fR: Scale to fill the entire output, cropping excess edges anchored at \fB--crop-gravity\fR (default).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfit\fR, \fBfit-border-color\fR, \fBcontain\fR: Scale to fit inside the output, padding letterbox/pillarbox bars with \fB--fill-color\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstretch\fR: Stretch non-uniformly to output dimensions.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcenter\fR, \fBno\fR: Center at 1:1 pixel resolution, padding surrounding space with \fB--fill-color\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtile\fR: Repeat image in a tiled grid across the output.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBspan\fR: Span a single panoramic canvas across the combined logical layout of all active monitors.
.RE
.PP
\fB--no-resize\fR
.RS 4
Center image at 1:1 pixel resolution without scaling (alias for \fB--resize no\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--crop-gravity\fR <GRAVITY>
.RS 4
Crop anchor when \fB--scaling-mode fill\fR (\fBcrop\fR) is active. Accepts \fBcenter\fR (\fBc\fR), \fBtop\fR (\fBnorth\fR, \fBn\fR, \fBt\fR), \fBbottom\fR (\fBsouth\fR, \fBs\fR, \fBb\fR), \fBleft\fR (\fBwest\fR, \fBw\fR, \fBl\fR), \fBright\fR (\fBeast\fR, \fBe\fR, \fBr\fR), \fBtop-left\fR (\fBtl\fR, \fBnw\fR, \fBnorthwest\fR), \fBtop-right\fR (\fBtr\fR, \fBne\fR, \fBnortheast\fR), \fBbottom-left\fR (\fBbl\fR, \fBsw\fR, \fBsouthwest\fR), \fBbottom-right\fR (\fBbr\fR, \fBse\fR, \fBsoutheast\fR), or normalized/percentage coordinates (\fB0.5,0.2\fR or \fB50%,20%\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--depth-map\fR <FILE>
.RS 4
Enable interactive 3D Parallax Occlusion Mapping (POM) on a 2D image using the grayscale depth map at \fIFILE\fR, driven by smoothed cursor tracking and workspace-slide inertia.
.RE
.PP
\fB--depth-strength\fR <FLOAT>
.RS 4
Depth parallax displacement multiplier when \fB--depth-map\fR is active (default: \fB1.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--fill-color\fR <HEX>
.RS 4
Background padding color in 6- or 8-digit hex for \fBfit\fR and \fBcenter\fR modes (default: \fB000000\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB-f, --filter\fR <Nearest|Bilinear|CatmullRom|Mitchell|Lanczos3>
.RS 4
Sampling filter hint for image scaling (\fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR compatibility).
.RE
.PP
\fB--no-cache\fR
.RS 4
Bypass cached transition/palette artifacts for this invocation.
.RE
.PP
\fB--clear-cache\fR
.RS 4
Purge cached transcodes and thumbnails before applying the new wallpaper.
.RE
.PP
\fB--10bit\fR
.RS 4
Request 10-bit wide-gamut scanout (\fBDRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010\fR / \fBDRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010\fR) and preserve 16-bit PNG/AVIF/JXL channel precision when supported by the compositor.
.RE
.PP
\fB--backdrop\fR <none|auto-blur|FILE>
.RS 4
Configure a secondary layer-shell surface with namespace \fBwaywal-backdrop\fR for compositors with overview backdrops such as Niri (\fBplace-within-backdrop true\fR). \fBauto-blur\fR renders a 2-pass Dual-Kawase Gaussian blur of the active wallpaper on the GPU at zero extra image-decode cost.
.RE
.PP
\fB--layer\fR <background|bottom>
.RS 4
Wayland layer-shell layer placement (default: \fBbackground\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--theme, --no-theme\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable automatic Material Design 3 OKLab/CAM16/HCT color extraction and \fBcaelestia\fR/\fBOSC\fR/template synchronization on wallpaper change.
.RE
.PP
\fB--theme-mode\fR <dark|light|auto>, \fB--dark\fR, \fB--light\fR
.RS 4
Select dark, light, or auto Material Design 3 tonal polarity (default: \fBdark\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--auto-day-night, --no-auto-day-night\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable automatic dark/light theme polarity switching based on astronomical solar elevation (\fB[solar]\fR latitude/longitude) or local time of day.
.RE
.PP
\fB--latitude\fR <DEG>, \fB--longitude\fR <DEG>
.RS 4
Observer latitude (\fB-90.0..90.0\fR) and longitude (\fB-180.0..180.0\fR) in decimal degrees for astronomical NOAA solar elevation calculations.
.RE
.PP
\fB--source-color-index\fR <0..3>
.RS 4
Select which of the 4 ranked K-Means++ seed clusters to use as the primary Material Design 3 seed (\fB0\fR = dominant, \fB1..3\fR = secondary/tertiary/quaternary accents).
.RE
.PP
\fB--seed-color\fR <HEX>
.RS 4
Override image color quantization with an explicit hex seed color (for example, \fB#89b4fa\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--theme-from-media, --no-theme-from-media\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable dynamic Material Design 3 palette extraction from active D-Bus \fBMPRIS2\fR album art.
.RE
.PP
\fB--animate\fR
.RS 4
Route animated GIF/WebP/APNG files through the hardware video/animation engine.
.RE
.PP
.SH VIDEO, SHADER & POWER OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-p, --prop\fR <KEY=VALUE>
.RS 4
Override a Wallpaper Engine Workshop user property when applying a scene (repeatable).
.RE
.PP
\fB--loop\fR <COUNT>
.RS 4
Number of playback loops for \fBvideo\fR (\fB0\fR for infinite loop, default: \fB0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--speed\fR <MULTIPLIER>
.RS 4
Playback speed multiplier for \fBvideo\fR and \fBshader\fR (default: \fB1.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--fps\fR <FPS>
.RS 4
Target rendering frame rate for \fBshader\fR and \fBworkshop\fR scenes (default: \fB60\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--audio\fR
.RS 4
Enable lock-free PipeWire default sink monitor capture and 64-bin logarithmic Bark-scale FFT uniforms (\fBu_audio_bands[64]\fR, \fBu_audio_envelope\fR, and Shadertoy \fBiChannel0\fR 512x2 audio texture) for \fBshader\fR and \fBworkshop\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fB--volume\fR <0.0..1.0>
.RS 4
Set wallpaper audio playback volume for \fBvideo\fR, \fBshader\fR, \fBworkshop\fR, and \fBaudio\fR (default: \fB0.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--mute-on-audio, --no-mute-on-audio\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable automatic exponential volume ducking when another application plays audio via PipeWire.
.RE
.PP
\fB--battery-policy\fR <ignore|reduce-fps|pause-video>
.RS 4
Configure the laptop battery governor policy when discharging or entering power-saver mode.
.RE
.PP
.SH SLIDESHOW OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-d, --interval, --duration\fR <DURATION>
.RS 4
Interval between slideshow transitions in seconds or human-readable units such as \fB30m\fR, \fB1h\fR, or \fB10m 30s\fR (default: \fB300\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB-s, --shuffle, --random\fR
.RS 4
Randomize slideshow traversal order using Fisher-Yates shuffling.
.RE
.PP
\fB--sort, --sorting\fR <ascending|descending|name|mtime|random>
.RS 4
Sort order for slideshow directory traversal (default: \fBascending\fR; \fBname\fR is an alias for \fBascending\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--recursive, --no-recursive\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable recursive subdirectory traversal when scanning a slideshow directory (default: \fB--recursive\fR).
.RE
.PP
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR
.RS 4
Wayland compositor socket name.
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Directory containing the \fBwwald\fR(1) IPC socket (\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wwald.sock\fR or \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/$WAYLAND_DISPLAY-wwald.<namespace>.sock\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBWWAL_CONFIG_PATH\fR
.RS 4
Location of \fBwwal/config.toml\fR (defaults to \fB~/.config/wwal/config.toml\fR), or explicit config file path override via \fBWWAL_CONFIG_PATH\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR, \fBWWAL_CACHE_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Location of \fBwwal/\fR generated color schemes, thumbnails, and cached transcodes (defaults to \fB~/.cache\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBXDG_STATE_HOME\fR, \fBWWAL_STATE_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Location of \fBwwal/state.bin\fR persistent output state (defaults to \fB~/.local/state\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_WORKSHOP_DIR\fR, \fBWWAL_WE_ASSETS_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Override path for Steam Workshop (\fB431960\fR) items and Wallpaper Engine default assets.
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_SHADER_PRESET_DIR\fR, \fBWWAL_SHADER_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Override directory path for built-in procedural shader preset files (\fB*.frag\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_NAMESPACE_PREFIX\fR
.RS 4
Optional namespace prefix filter when broadcasting commands with \fB-a, --all\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fBSWWW_NAMESPACE\fR, \fBAWWW_NAMESPACE\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_FPS\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_FPS\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_STEP\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_STEP\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_DURATION\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_DURATION\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_ANGLE\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_ANGLE\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_POS\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_POS\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_BEZIER\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_BEZIER\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_WAVE\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_WAVE\fR, \fBSWWW_INVERT_Y\fR, \fBAWWW_INVERT_Y\fR, \fBSWWW_TRANSITION_INVERT_Y\fR, \fBAWWW_TRANSITION_INVERT_Y\fR, \fBSWWW_CROP_GRAVITY\fR, \fBAWWW_CROP_GRAVITY\fR, \fBSWWW_FILTER\fR, \fBAWWW_FILTER\fR, \fBSWWW_RESIZE\fR, \fBAWWW_RESIZE\fR, \fBSWWW_FILL_COLOR\fR, \fBAWWW_FILL_COLOR\fR, \fBSWWW_OUTPUTS\fR, \fBAWWW_OUTPUTS\fR
.RS 4
Drop-in \fBswww\fR / \fBawww\fR v0.12.1 environment variable overrides.
.RE
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
\fB~/.config/wwal/config.toml\fR
.RS 4
Declarative daemon, theme, template, solar/schedule, transition, output, and workspace configuration. See \fBwwal-config\fR(5).
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.local/state/caelestia/scheme.json\fR
.RS 4
Material Design 3 tonal palette output for Quickshell (\fBcaelestia-shell\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.cache/wwal/colors.json\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors.css\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/colors-hyprland.conf\fR
.RS 4
Exported OKLab/HCT palette files for Waybar, GTK, and Hyprland.
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.cache/wal/colors.json\fR, \fB~/.cache/wal/colors\fR, \fB~/.cache/wal/colors.sh\fR, \fB~/.cache/wal/colors.css\fR, \fB~/.cache/wal/sequences\fR
.RS 4
Pywal and Pywalfox compatibility palette files.
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.cache/wwal/current_wallpaper\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/current_wallpaper.png\fR
.RS 4
Symlink to the active wallpaper and pre-rendered lockscreen PNG frame (\fB<= 1280x720\fR) for \fBhyprlock\fR and \fBswaylock\fR.
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.cache/wwal/thumbs/\fR, \fB~/.cache/wwal/workshop-previews/\fR
.RS 4
Cached picker thumbnails and human-readable Steam Workshop preview symlinks.
.RE
.PP
\fB~/.cache/swww/<output>\fR, \fB~/.cache/awww/<output>\fR
.RS 4
Drop-in \fBswww\fR/\fBawww\fR per-output state cache files.
.RE
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Set a wallpaper with a 144 FPS circular iris transition anchored at the cursor and extract a Material You palette:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal img ~/Pictures/cyberpunk.avif --transition-type grow --transition-pos cursor --transition-fps 144 --theme
.RE
.fi
.PP
Launch the unified icon-grid wallpaper picker (Rofi / Fuzzel / Walker):
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal pick
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run a built-in procedural shader preset with PipeWire audio reactivity:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal shader preset audio_bars --audio
.RE
.fi
.PP
Sync Steam Workshop preview symlinks for \fBwaypaper\fR and apply a Workshop scene:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
wwal workshop sync-previews
wwal workshop apply 2841902341
.RE
.fi
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBwwald\fR(1), \fBwwal-config\fR(5)
